WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.126 --> 00:00:03.670
Hey, guys. It's me Issa Rae,
and I am joined

00:00:03.753 --> 00:00:07.173
by our incredibly talented
showrunner, Prentice Penny,

00:00:07.257 --> 00:00:09.342
for another season
of our Wine Down.

00:00:09.551 --> 00:00:12.303
♪ (UPTEMPO MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:12.929 --> 00:00:15.849
So, the cold open ends
with Issa saying

00:00:15.932 --> 00:00:17.684
she doesn't "eff" with Molly
no more.

00:00:17.767 --> 00:00:19.978
How does this set the tone
for the new season?

00:00:20.061 --> 00:00:22.147
We've been building
to Issa and Molly needing

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:23.148
to have a conversation.

00:00:23.231 --> 00:00:25.108
And we want the audience
to be like,

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:26.693
"What-- What did I miss?"

00:00:26.776 --> 00:00:28.027
Our show is known as--
you know,

00:00:28.111 --> 00:00:29.988
for Issa
and Molly's relationship,

00:00:30.071 --> 00:00:31.030
they are legit friends.

00:00:31.114 --> 00:00:32.657
They're girls.
They ride for each other.

00:00:32.741 --> 00:00:34.159
We wanted to start to question:

00:00:34.242 --> 00:00:36.786
"Are these friendships
or relationships for a reason,

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:37.912
or for a season?"

00:00:37.996 --> 00:00:39.539
So, one of the things
that's a big deal

00:00:39.622 --> 00:00:41.374
is how everybody's like
leveling up this year.

00:00:41.458 --> 00:00:45.670
Well, Issa and Molly start off
as we see them, together, uh,

00:00:45.754 --> 00:00:47.213
-taking care of themselves.
-Yep.

00:00:47.297 --> 00:00:49.716
And I think Issa,
more so than Molly,

00:00:49.799 --> 00:00:53.803
has decided to focus
on nothing but good vibes.

00:00:53.887 --> 00:00:57.390
Making sure that her career
or her passion is in order.

00:00:57.474 --> 00:01:01.436
And not letting distractions,
uh, take her away from that.

00:01:01.519 --> 00:01:03.563
I think also too,
like what we've done, too,

00:01:03.646 --> 00:01:05.523
is I think tried to flip
the season a little bit.

00:01:05.607 --> 00:01:08.234
The dynamics where like,
"Oh, Issa has a lot of work--

00:01:08.318 --> 00:01:09.444
-Yeah.
-...situations,

00:01:09.527 --> 00:01:12.030
and Molly is having
more personal, men issues."

00:01:12.113 --> 00:01:14.783
They've tasked each other
to hold each other accountable.

00:01:15.033 --> 00:01:17.702
And we found out at the end
of the episode that...

00:01:17.786 --> 00:01:20.705
-(WINCES)
-...maybe Issa's not ready

00:01:20.789 --> 00:01:23.374
for Molly to hold her
so accountable,

00:01:23.458 --> 00:01:25.210
and to be so truthful.
Um...

00:01:25.293 --> 00:01:28.296
It's almost like, uh,
be careful what you wish for.

00:01:28.379 --> 00:01:30.590
Yeah. So,
throughout the series,

00:01:30.673 --> 00:01:34.636
we haven't seen Molly
be in a long-term relation--

00:01:34.719 --> 00:01:35.929
-No.
-Her relationships.

00:01:36.012 --> 00:01:37.889
-She blows those up.
-Yeah! (CHUCKLES)

00:01:37.972 --> 00:01:39.224
They kind of fizzle.

00:01:39.307 --> 00:01:43.311
I think, inherently, her nature,
is to want to be boo'd up.

00:01:43.394 --> 00:01:45.188
-I think she's fighting...
-Yeah.

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:46.648
...that energy
to want to do that.

00:01:46.731 --> 00:01:50.151
And I think when she realizes,
like, "Oh, he's dating too."

00:01:50.235 --> 00:01:51.820
Which is what you said
you were doing, it's like,

00:01:51.903 --> 00:01:53.279
"I don't really want you
to be out there...

00:01:53.363 --> 00:01:54.280
-Exactly.
-...I'm out there."

00:01:54.614 --> 00:01:56.407
Despite her denial,
she's invested in Andrew--

00:01:56.491 --> 00:01:57.700
-For sure. Yes
-...at this point.

00:01:57.784 --> 00:02:00.078
And I think it was a big step
for her to text him.

00:02:00.161 --> 00:02:00.995
-Yep.
-And...

00:02:01.329 --> 00:02:03.498
I'm curious, like,
why do you think Molly comes

00:02:03.581 --> 00:02:06.000
for Issa after finding out
that she's gonna

00:02:06.084 --> 00:02:07.961
continue working
with Condola,

00:02:08.211 --> 00:02:11.047
despite the fact that Condola
is dating Lawrence?

00:02:11.422 --> 00:02:16.594
Molly, knowing Issa's history,
I think she knows more

00:02:16.678 --> 00:02:18.221
about Issa
and Lawrence's relationship

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:19.305
-than anyone.
-Yeah.

00:02:19.556 --> 00:02:21.766
Molly knows that Issa's
ultimately gonna be affected

00:02:21.850 --> 00:02:23.476
-by this.
-Molly knows all this stuff

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:24.727
about you as a friend,

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:26.229
and Condola doesn't know
anything.

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:28.022
And Condola's energy
is just to want to build you up,

00:02:28.106 --> 00:02:29.649
so that's infectious, right?

00:02:29.732 --> 00:02:31.234
Like, you're already feeling

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:32.694
-like planning this is a lot.
-Yeah.

00:02:32.777 --> 00:02:34.237
And here comes this woman
believing in you

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:35.905
while this other friend
is kind of like,

00:02:36.239 --> 00:02:38.825
-"Girl, this is a mess."
-That is so real too.

00:02:38.908 --> 00:02:40.243
And we've talked about this
in the room.

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:41.786
is that Issa is the type
of person

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:45.081
to feed off of people putting
that kind of energy in her.

00:02:45.164 --> 00:02:45.915
Yep.

00:02:46.165 --> 00:02:47.876
Like, she needs that
to kind of succeed.

00:02:47.959 --> 00:02:51.170
In some ways you need
stupidity around you...

00:02:51.254 --> 00:02:53.464
-(LAUGHS)
-...to-- Because--

00:02:53.548 --> 00:02:55.466
Like the first person to fly,
he's going,

00:02:55.550 --> 00:02:56.426
"I'ma do what that bird does."

00:02:56.634 --> 00:02:58.511
-It's like, "Fool, don't."
-Yeah, "Don't."

00:02:58.595 --> 00:02:59.679
"Don't, you ain't gonna fly."

00:03:00.013 --> 00:03:01.180
-But that person next to you...
-But you need to believe--

00:03:01.264 --> 00:03:02.849
...is like, "Yeah, bruh, fly."

00:03:02.932 --> 00:03:04.976
-"You could fly!"
-"You could fly!" Like--

00:03:05.059 --> 00:03:07.020
Why do you feel Issa
has the need

00:03:07.103 --> 00:03:10.356
to tell these potential sponsors
different versions

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:12.108
of what the block party
should be?

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:15.194
(SIGHS) Issa's always
just trying to sell some shit.

00:03:15.278 --> 00:03:19.282
It's just-- Honesty is not
her favorite policy.

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:20.116
Yeah.

00:03:20.491 --> 00:03:23.411
And I think this comes
from this feeling of like,

00:03:23.494 --> 00:03:24.871
"Maybe my event
isn't good enough.

00:03:24.954 --> 00:03:26.915
Maybe I'm not the right person
to do this,

00:03:26.998 --> 00:03:29.208
so I need to tell them
what they want to hear.

00:03:29.292 --> 00:03:32.378
As opposed to having them buy in
to who I am,

00:03:32.462 --> 00:03:34.881
because maybe who I am
isn't enough."

00:03:34.964 --> 00:03:36.883
You know, in the end,
they bought into her.

00:03:36.966 --> 00:03:38.509
Like when you're throwing
an event like this,

00:03:38.593 --> 00:03:40.470
nobody's like, really like,

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:41.888
"Oh, this event
is the dopest thing,"

00:03:41.971 --> 00:03:43.056
or, "This is the best idea."

00:03:43.139 --> 00:03:44.474
-They're really looking at you.
-Yeah.

00:03:44.557 --> 00:03:46.434
They're like,
"What is it about you

00:03:46.517 --> 00:03:48.227
that I should put my money
behind?"

00:03:48.311 --> 00:03:50.438
And I think she realizes that
later.

00:03:50.521 --> 00:03:52.398
-This is a good season.
-It is gonna be good.

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:55.026
Thank you for hanging out
with us tonight.

00:03:55.109 --> 00:03:56.069
See you next week.

00:03:56.152 --> 00:03:58.613
-Next week, cheers.
-Cheers!

00:03:59.322 --> 00:04:00.990
♪ (MUSIC CONCLUDES) ♪

